{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-332952" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=9x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =1\\pm 6\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074855/state.json" "file_sha256" "6adc22ae3dcffbfe6f82f7fadbaa81db5f7151f0edcc1c41881d7857ce24fbb5"} {"question" "q-332952" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that $a=\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=1>0$ and ${e}^{at}={e}^{t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, we have a spiral that is traversed toward infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nTherefore, since $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0,$ the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable spiral (source)}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074855/state.json" "file_sha256" "6adc22ae3dcffbfe6f82f7fadbaa81db5f7151f0edcc1c41881d7857ce24fbb5"} {"question" "q-332952" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074855/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e10af81c6d18ae6b4c97703723178066d14dbecd11dbb31144a68f1389db02fa"} {"question" "q-332952" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074855/state.json" "file_sha256" "6adc22ae3dcffbfe6f82f7fadbaa81db5f7151f0edcc1c41881d7857ce24fbb5"} {"question" "q-332952" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )<0"] ["math" "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=0"] ["math" "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )>0"] ["math" "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )<0"] ["math" "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0"] ["math" "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074855/state.json" "file_sha256" "6adc22ae3dcffbfe6f82f7fadbaa81db5f7151f0edcc1c41881d7857ce24fbb5"} {"question" "q-332952" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074855/state.json" "file_sha256" "6adc22ae3dcffbfe6f82f7fadbaa81db5f7151f0edcc1c41881d7857ce24fbb5"} {"question" "q-332952" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/