e that the given curve is $\\text{unbounded},$ representing $\\text{a spiral}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$ Thus, we must have $a\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, notice that the spiral is traversed toward $\\text{the origin}.$\n\nHence, to insure that ${e}^{at}\\to 0,$ we require $a<0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074855/state.json" "file_sha256" "6adc22ae3dcffbfe6f82f7fadbaa81db5f7151f0edcc1c41881d7857ce24fbb5"} {"question" "q-334285" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074855/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e10af81c6d18ae6b4c97703723178066d14dbecd11dbb31144a68f1389db02fa"} {"question" "q-334285" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074855/state.json" "file_sha256" "6adc22ae3dcffbfe6f82f7fadbaa81db5f7151f0edcc1c41881d7857ce24fbb5"} {"question" "q-334285" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "bounded"] ["text" "unbounded"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074855/state.json" "file_sha256" "6adc22ae3dcffbfe6f82f7fadbaa81db5f7151f0edcc1c41881d7857ce24fbb5"} {"question" "q-334285" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "unbounded"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074855/state.json" "file_sha256" "6adc22ae3dcffbfe6f82f7fadbaa81db5f7151f0edcc1c41881d7857ce24fbb5"} {"question" "q-334285" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/typ